course: dictionary
lesson: 10181
title: Tightness: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the clues around it tell you which one is meant. Tightness is a noun that comes from tight. «Bouncing in a stretch can pull the muscle; ease in slowly to a feeling of mild tightness, not pain, and hold still for about 20 seconds.» Here tightness is a feeling in your muscles, not a shoe that is too small.
explain: Ask yourself: what is being tight, and what kind of tight? A rope has tightness when it is pulled hard. Your chest has tightness when it feels squeezed. A team has tightness when its members stick together and are loyal to each other. Money has tightness when there is very little to spare.
explain: Some tightness is a warning. Sudden chest tightness, especially with pain or trouble breathing, needs an adult straight away, and maybe emergency help. If you have asthma, chest tightness can be a sign to use your inhaler. Always tell an adult when your body feels wrong.
fact: Tightness means being tight, or a feeling of being squeezed or stiff.
fact: «Tightness» has four main meanings: fitting closely, a feeling in the body, closeness within a group, and very little money to spare.
fact: Muscle tightness can be eased by stretching slowly, not by bouncing.
fact: Sudden chest tightness with pain or trouble breathing needs an adult and maybe emergency help.
fact: Tightness is uncountable, so you do not say two tightnesses; you say the tightness.
exercise: «Ease in slowly to a feeling of mild tightness, not pain, when you stretch.» What does tightness mean here? | A sharp pain that stops you moving | A loud noise from the muscle | *A feeling of being stretched or squeezed in the muscle | A cold, wet feeling
exercise: Priya says, «I have great tightness of money, so I can buy anything.» What does tightness of money really mean? | Lots of money to spend | Money pulled hard like a rope | *Very little money to spare | Money hidden in a box
exercise: A team with great tightness always sticks together. What kind of tightness does the team have? | Being very cold | *Closeness and loyalty as a group | Fitting very closely, like tight shoes | A pain in the chest
test: Which meaning fits the tightness of a rope? | Feeling sad and stiff | Hidden under the bed | Full of water and soft | *Pulled hard and firmly fixed
test: A friend has sudden chest tightness and trouble breathing. What should you do? | Keep running until it stops | *Tell an adult straight away | Wait a week to see | Bounce on the spot to stretch it
exam: In a story, «a tightness in her throat» most likely shows what? | Bright colours | Hunger | *Worry | Being very fast
